# Naming Conventions

## Files

All files use **kebab-case**.

| Type | File pattern | Export pattern |
|---|---|---|
| Components | `dashboard-{feature}-{role}.tsx` | `PascalCase` |
| Hooks (query) | `use-{resource}.ts` | `use{Resource}()` |
| Hooks (mutation) | `use-{action}.ts` | `use{Action}()` |
| Hooks (dashboard, cross-cutting) | `use-{scope}-{behavior}.ts` in `apps/dashboard/src/hooks/` | `use{Scope}{Behavior}()` |
| Stores (dashboard) | `store.ts` in `apps/dashboard/src/shared/lib/{domain}/` | `create()` store + selectors |
| Utilities | `{name}.ts` | camelCase functions |
| Schema files | `{entity}.ts` | see Schema Naming below |

## Components

- File: `dashboard-library-analysis.tsx`
- Export: `DashboardLibraryAnalysis`
- Always co-locate a skeleton: `DashboardLibraryAnalysisSkeleton`
- `"use client"` only when browser APIs, event handlers, or hooks are used

## Schema Naming (Zod)

- Input schemas: `{entity}{Action}Input` — e.g. `playlistGetByIdInput`
- Output schemas: `{entity}{Action}OutputSchema` — e.g. `playlistGetByIdOutputSchema`
- Inferred types: `type PlaylistGetById = z.infer<typeof playlistGetByIdOutputSchema>`
- Enums: `{entity}{Field}Enum` — e.g. `pipelineStatusEnum`
- Metadata schemas: `{entity}MetadataSchema` — e.g. `playlistMetadataSchema`

## Import Aliases

Within each app (`api`, `dashboard`, `web`, `admin`), use `@/*` for local imports:
```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { useDashboardPipelineBootstrap } from "@/hooks/use-dashboard-pipeline-bootstrap";
```

Across packages, use workspace package names:
```typescript
import { db } from "@harmonia/db";
import { track } from "@harmonia/db/schema/track";
import { env } from "@harmonia/env/server";
import { dashboardAuth, adminAuth } from "@harmonia/core";
import { logger } from "@harmonia/logger";
```

## Constants

`UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for module-level constants:
```typescript
const MAX_TRACKS_PER_ARTIST = 4;
const EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE = 64;
```

Only export a constant into a package's `constants/*.ts` file if it's used from 2+ files. A constant used in exactly one file stays local to that file (unexported, no separate constants-file entry).

## Commits

`feat:` `fix:` `chore:` `perf:` `refactor:` prefixes. No scope required.

No AI/tool branding in commit messages or PR text; no `Co-authored-by:` for assistants (see project overview).
